# Database / media
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
# Unanchored on purpose. This was `/media/`, which only ever matched a media directory at the
# repository root — and the one that actually fills up is
# src/backend/Crusaders.Mainframe.Api/media/, written by any local run of the API. It held real
# uploaded member photographs and was fully tracked-eligible, so a `git add -A` would have
# committed members' faces.
media/

# Secrets — defensive (never commit local secrets even if named oddly)
*.pem
*.pfx
secrets.json

# Scratch — every temporary artefact (logs, screenshots, captures, reports).
# Emptied at the end of every session; see the tree root CLAUDE.md "Scratch" section.
.tmp/

# Agent worktrees. `git worktree add .claude/worktrees/<name>` puts a whole second
# checkout inside this one; git reports it as a single untracked directory, so a
# `git add -A` in the main checkout offers to commit it as an embedded repository.
# Scoped to `worktrees/` rather than to `.claude/`, so a settings file somebody does
# want tracked is still visible to `git status`.
.claude/worktrees/

# IoT firmware (src/iot) — build output, toolchain venv, coverage
src/iot/.pio/
src/iot/.venv/
src/iot/coverage.xml
src/iot/**/*.bin
src/iot/**/*.elf
src/iot/**/*.hex

# iCloud's fabricated numbered duplicates inside the generated Arduino sketches.
# This checkout is on an iCloud Drive path and iCloud invents `Name 2.h` /
# `Name 3.cpp` copies of files it has just seen written. Inside a sketch's src/
# the Arduino IDE COMPILES them, and 27 of them were committed once before this
# rule existed. `make arduino-export` also deletes them; belt and braces.
src/iot/arduino/**/* [0-9]*.*
src/iot/arduino/**/* [0-9]

# Firmware secrets — a filled-in secrets.h was previously committable.
# Two copies exist by design and both are covered by this one rule:
#   src/iot/src/common/secrets.h                    the PlatformIO build's
#   src/iot/arduino/court_bridge/secrets.h          the Arduino IDE sketch's
# Their .example siblings ARE committed.
**/secrets.h
**/ota_privkey.pem

